Phase 1 — Basic

The Basic phase focuses on creating the initial application structure, user interface, and navigation. At this stage, the main goal is to create the basic screens of the application using Kotlin and XML.

Features

1. Login & Sign Up
Users will be able to access the application through Login and create a new account through the Sign Up screen.

2. Home/Dashboard
The home screen will provide an overview of the user's health information, such as BMI, calories, and steps.

3. Community
A basic community section will allow users to see posts related to health and fitness.

4. Like & Comment
Users will be able to like posts and add comments to community posts.

Technologies
Android Studio
Kotlin
XML
Material Design

Main goal: Create the basic screens and navigation of the application.

🟡 Phase 2 — Intermediate

The Intermediate phase focuses on making the basic screens functional and connecting the application with databases and external services.

Features

1. Firebase Authentication
Users will be able to create accounts and securely log in using Firebase Authentication.

2. User Profile
Users will be able to store information such as name, age, height, weight, and other basic details.

3. BMI Calculator
The application will calculate BMI based on the user's height and weight and display the result.

4. Food Tracker
Users will be able to record their daily food intake, including calories, protein, carbohydrates, and fats.

5. Step Counter
The application will use the phone's sensors to track the user's daily steps.

6. Community System
Users will be able to create posts, like posts, and write comments. The data will be stored online.

7. Barcode Scanner
Users will be able to scan packaged food barcodes and retrieve nutritional information.

8. Food Database
The application will use the Open Food Facts API to retrieve information such as calories, protein, fat, and carbohydrates.

Technologies
Firebase Authentication
Firebase Cloud Firestore
Room Database
Android SensorManager
Google ML Kit Barcode Scanning
Open Food Facts REST API

Main goal: Convert the Basic UI into a functional health and diet monitoring application.

🔴 Phase 3 — Final

The Final phase focuses on adding the AI/ML features, health integration, analytics, and final improvements.

Features

1. AI-Based Food Recommendation
The application will recommend suitable foods or meals based on user information, health goals, calorie requirements, and food data.

2. Machine Learning Model
A machine learning model will be trained using Python and Scikit-learn. The trained model will later be converted to TensorFlow Lite for use inside the Android application.

3. Personalized Recommendations
The application will provide recommendations based on individual user goals, such as weight management or maintaining a healthy diet.

4. Health Connect Integration
Health-related activity information can be integrated through Android Health Connect.

5. Progress Tracking & Charts
The application will display calorie intake, steps, weight, and other progress using graphs and charts.

6. Final UI & Testing
The application interface will be improved using Material Design 3. The complete application will then be tested, bugs will be fixed, and the final APK will be generated.

Technologies
Python
Scikit-learn
TensorFlow Lite
Health Connect SDK
MPAndroidChart
Material Design 3
Git & GitHub
Android Studio

Main goal: Add AI-powered recommendations, health integration, analytics, and prepare the application for final deployment.
